<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lielupe</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lielupe is a river of central Latvia, formed near Bauska by the meeting of the Mūša and Mēmele, which rise in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>. It flows about 119 km across the Zemgale plain to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-riga">Gulf of Riga</a> near Jūrmala. Its basin was the heartland of the medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/semigallians">Semigallians</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lielupe.jpg" alt="Lielupe" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lazdynas at Lithuanian Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:4208LielupeMezotne.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
